The filing reports that comparable sales decreased 2.6 percent in fiscal 2025, driven by a 2.2 percent decrease in traffic and a 0.4 percent decrease in average transaction amount. [1] So the decline came mostly from fewer transactions, with a smaller contribution from lower spending per transaction.

By channel, stores originated comparable sales fell 4.0 percent, while digitally originated comparable sales rose 3.1 percent. [2] The filing also shows that digitally originated sales made up 20.6 percent of merchandise sales, up from 19.6 percent the prior year. [2]

The filing does not give a fuller causal explanation. It says the interaction of macroeconomic, competitive, and consumer behavioral factors, along with sales mix and transfers of sales between stores and channels, makes further analysis of sales metrics infeasible. [3]